RefuseRefuse currently runs as a browser-first app with a FastAPI backend and a Vite frontend.

Quick start

- `npm run dev` to restart services and stream logs
- `npm run status` to confirm backend/frontend are running
- Open `http://localhost:5173`

For full setup, run commands, and architecture notes, use `ARCHITECTURE.md` as the source of truth.

Current local workflow

- `make start` starts the backend on `http://localhost:8000` and the frontend on `http://localhost:5173`
- `make stop` stops both services
- `make status` shows whether both services are running
- `npm run start` and `npm run status` mirror the Make targets from the repo root

Project layout

- `backend/` contains the FastAPI API and local SQLite data
- `frontend/` contains the Vite browser app
- `mobile/` contains the Expo mobile app shell

Mobile plan

The earlier Expo scaffold was intentionally removed from the repo root so the active app stayed unambiguous. Mobile now lives in its own dedicated `mobile/` directory instead of sharing the root with the browser app.

Mobile quick start

- `cd mobile && npm install`
- `npm run mobile:start` from the repo root, or `npm start` inside `mobile/`
- Set `EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` if you are running on a device instead of a simulator

Social auth quick setup

- Copy and customize env templates:
	- `backend/.env.example`
	- `frontend/.env.example`
	- `mobile/.env.example`
- Backend must be started with `GOOGLE_CLIENT_IDS` and `APPLE_AUDIENCES` configured.
- Frontend uses Google and Apple JS SDKs and exchanges provider ID tokens with backend OAuth endpoints.
- Mobile uses Expo Google/Apple sign-in and exchanges provider ID tokens with backend OAuth endpoints.
